The files under proto/ are an UNMODIFIED COPY of that repository's proto/zmk/
directory. They define the message format spoken by ZMK Studio and by every
ZMK keyboard with Studio enabled.

DO NOT EDIT THESE FILES BY HAND.

They are someone else's contract. Editing our copy makes it silently disagree with
what keyboards actually speak, which means decoding a shape that no keyboard sends. To change anything here, change the pinned revision - see ../../scripts/reconcile_zmk_model/README.md.

The generated Python bindings in ../../zmk_studio_client/_pb/ are derived from these files and
carry the same copyright and licence in their headers. Unlike this directory they are
packaged and distributed, so the attribution has to travel in the files themselves;
src/scripts/reconcile_zmk_model/reconcile.sh re-applies it after every regeneration.

Not vendored: upstream also ships *.options.in files, which are nanopb size constraints
used when compiling the firmware. They affect neither the wire format nor Python decoding.
